+    /// Queue-saturation early termination (Patience; Teofili and Lin, ECIR
+    /// 2025), bounded-queue path only. A counter tracks how many times a point
+    /// has entered the watched queue so far. After each expanded candidate the
+    /// counter is compared with its value after the previous expansion; the
+    /// expansion counts as saturated when previous / current >= patience_s.
+    /// When more than patience_p expansions in a row are saturated, the search
+    /// stops before the next candidate is popped. ORed with the other stopping
+    /// conditions. patience_p = 0 disables it and leaves faiss untouched.
+    /// patience_queue selects the watched queue:
+    ///   0 = the efSearch nearest points whose distance has been computed
+    ///       (an auxiliary max-heap; the queue is the beam),
+    ///   1 = the result heap (a point enters when res.add_result accepts it).
+    int patience_p = 0;
+    double patience_s = 0.995;
+    int patience_queue = 0;
+
